From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alan Bradburne <abradburne@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 22:06:45 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] power: supply: rk817: refresh plug state in rk817_read_props

rk817_charger only updates charger->plugged_in at probe and from its
plug-in and plug-out threaded IRQs. If a plug event is missed (for
example across suspend), online and the charger LED trigger stay stale
indefinitely, even though rk817_resume() immediately runs
rk817_read_props() and the monitor polls every 8 seconds.

Check RK817_SYS_STS (RK817_PLUG_IN_STS) in rk817_read_props() and, when
it disagrees with charger->plugged_in, update it, reapply the charge
voltage (and USB input limits on unplug, as rk817_plug_out_isr() does),
and notify both power supplies.

Upstream status: candidate.
---
 drivers/power/supply/rk817_charger.c | 29 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 29 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/rk817_charger.c b/drivers/power/supply/rk817_charger.c
index 81c0123..e028b00 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/rk817_charger.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/rk817_charger.c
@@ -367,6 +367,35 @@ static void rk817_read_props(struct rk817_charger *charger)
 {
 	int tmp, reg;
 	u8 bulk_reg[4];
+	bool plugged_in;
+
+	/*
+	 * Refresh the plug state from hardware in case a plug-in or plug-out
+	 * interrupt was missed (for instance across suspend).
+	 */
+	if (!regmap_read(charger->rk808->regmap, RK817_SYS_STS, &reg)) {
+		plugged_in = !!(reg & RK817_PLUG_IN_STS);
+		if (plugged_in != !!charger->plugged_in) {
+			charger->plugged_in = plugged_in;
+			rk817_set_chg_volt(charger);
+			if (!plugged_in) {
+				regmap_write_bits(charger->rk808->regmap,
+						  RK817_PMIC_CHRG_IN,
+						  RK817_USB_VLIM_SEL, (0x05 << 4));
+				regmap_write_bits(charger->rk808->regmap,
+						  RK817_PMIC_CHRG_IN,
+						  RK817_USB_VLIM_EN, (0x01 << 7));
+				regmap_write_bits(charger->rk808->regmap,
+						  RK817_PMIC_CHRG_IN,
+						  RK817_USB_ILIM_SEL, 0x03);
+				regmap_write_bits(charger->rk808->regmap,
+						  RK817_PMIC_CHRG_IN,
+						  RK817_USB_ILIM_EN, (0x01 << 3));
+			}
+			power_supply_changed(charger->chg_ps);
+			power_supply_changed(charger->bat_ps);
+		}
+	}
 
 	/*
 	 * Recalibrate voltage and current readings if we need to BSP does both
